---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Contact | PubMed Trivia"
  description="Contact PubMed Trivia for corrections, partnership inquiries, media requests, or questions about our medical research summaries."
  lang="en"
>
  <article>
    <h1>Contact</h1>

    <p>
      We welcome questions, feedback, and corrections from readers, researchers, and institutions.
      PubMed Trivia is an independent content outlet that summarizes and reviews peer-reviewed
      research from PubMed in biology, medicine, and psychology. Whether you have spotted an error
      in one of our summaries, want to collaborate on content, or have a partnership idea,
      the email address below is the right place to reach us. We do not accept inquiries via
      social-media DMs or on-site comment threads.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Email</h2>
    <p>
      For all general inquiries &mdash; content corrections, media requests, partnership
      proposals, or reader feedback &mdash; please use:
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong><a href="mailto:sciencepubmedjp@gmail.com">sciencepubmedjp@gmail.com</a></strong>
    </p>
    <p>
      We read every message but do not send automated replies. Responses typically take
      a few days up to one week. To help us route your message efficiently, please include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your name (a pseudonym is fine)</li>
      <li>Type of inquiry (correction, media, partnership, other)</li>
      <li>The URL of the relevant article, if applicable</li>
      <li>A clear description of the question or feedback</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We cannot respond to medical emergencies. If you have urgent health concerns, please
      contact a qualified medical professional or emergency services in your jurisdiction.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Corrections and fact-checking</h2>
    <p>
      PubMed Trivia summarizes peer-reviewed articles indexed in PubMed, but errors can creep
      into translation, summarization, or editorial work. If you spot a factual mistake,
      a mismatch between our summary and the original paper, a broken link, or a typographic
      issue, please let us know. When we revise an article in response to feedback, we append
      a <strong>Correction Log</strong> at the bottom of the page noting what changed and when.
      See our <a href="/en/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a> for details on how we handle
      updates, retractions, and withdrawn studies.
    </p>
    <p>
      If a paper we have summarized is later retracted or flagged with an Expression of
      Concern on PubMed, please notify us so we can update the on-site notice promptly.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Media, partnerships, and advertising</h2>
    <p>
      PubMed Trivia is an independent publication focused on peer-reviewed medical, biological,
      and psychological research. We consider inquiries in the following categories:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Advertising and sponsored content from health, medical, and life-science companies
          (clearly labeled, subject to our editorial standards)</li>
      <li>Collaboration with research institutions, universities, and academic publishers</li>
      <li>Reprint and citation requests from other media outlets (case by case)</li>
      <li>Reader suggestions for topics or research areas to cover</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      All sponsored content is clearly disclosed. We reserve the right to decline placements
      that conflict with our <a href="/en/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a> or that
      promote claims without adequate scientific support. See our
      <a href="/en/disclosure/">Advertising and Affiliate Disclosure</a> for details on how
      we handle paid placements and affiliate links.
    </p>

    <h2>4. What we cannot answer</h2>
    <p>
      We are not clinicians, and PubMed Trivia is a research-summary outlet rather than a
      medical service. For your safety, we do not respond to the following:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Individual medical advice (diagnosis, treatment plans, medication questions)</li>
      <li>Recommendations about specific supplements, drugs, or interventions</li>
      <li>Requests for the contact details of study authors or research institutions
          (please consult the paper on PubMed directly)</li>
      <li>Paid article-translation or custom-summary requests</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you have a health concern, please consult a qualified medical professional.
      Our articles are summaries of published research and, as our
      <a href="/en/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a> makes clear, they are not a
      substitute for professional medical advice.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Related pages</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/en/about/">About PubMed Trivia</a></li>
      <li><a href="/en/editor/">Editor profile</a></li>
      <li><a href="/en/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a></li>
      <li><a href="/en/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a></li>
      <li><a href="/en/disclosure/">Advertising and Affiliate Disclosure</a></li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      <small>Last updated: 18 November 2026</small>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
